# Backend proxy target — already set; keep as-is.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://financestreamai-backend.onrender.com/api/v1

# ─── NextAuth / Google sign-in (REQUIRED) ────────────────────────────────
# All four vars below are REQUIRED for sign-in to work.
# Without them the "Sign in" button appears to do nothing on production
# because NextAuth silently 500s /api/auth/csrf and /api/auth/signin/google.
#
# Debug endpoint: GET /api/auth/diagnose returns which vars are missing
# (booleans only — no values leaked).

# 1) From https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#    → OAuth 2.0 Client IDs → Web application
#    Authorized JavaScript origins:
#       http://localhost:3000
#       https://<your-vercel-domain>          (e.g. stockwiz-ai-web.vercel.app)
#    Authorized redirect URIs (BOTH, exact):
#       http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google
#       https://<your-vercel-domain>/api/auth/callback/google
#
#    Also on Google Cloud Console → OAuth consent screen:
#      - If in "Testing" mode, add your Gmail as a Test User, OR
#      - Publish the app (may require verification for sensitive scopes).
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# 2) Random 32-byte secret. Generate with one of:
#    PowerShell: [Convert]::ToBase64String((1..32 | ForEach-Object { Get-Random -Maximum 256 }))
#    OpenSSL   : openssl rand -base64 32
#    Node      : node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=

# 3) For local dev:  http://localhost:3000
#    For Vercel prod: set to your production URL (e.g. https://stockwiz-ai-web.vercel.app).
#    On Vercel, also set the same three vars above in the Vercel dashboard
#    (Project → Settings → Environment Variables) — .env.local is gitignored
#    and NOT deployed.
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
